From 496ec989efd266deff2003afbc30790086679294 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:08:40 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 28/38] qt: do not empty the window for a widget that has no
 size yet

Showing a widget of the central stack restored the size remembered for
it, and the video widget shown for the first time has none: the map
gave an invalid size of -1x-1. In normal view that only took one pixel
off the window's frame, but in minimal view the stack is the whole
window, which was resized to nothing. Qt hides a window that has no
size, and on Wayland hiding a window destroys its surface: the video's
native child (the stereo video layer) was a subsurface of that surface,
Qt kept moving it after the window got a new one, and the compositor
ended the connection ("wl_subsurface: error 0: no parent"). VLC Stereo
died at the start of every video in minimal view, 2D ones too.

Restore only a size the widget had; the video widget sets its own size
right after.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 modules/gui/qt/main_interface.cpp | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/modules/gui/qt/main_interface.cpp b/modules/gui/qt/main_interface.cpp
index 729e47e..680c3fc 100644
--- a/modules/gui/qt/main_interface.cpp
+++ b/modules/gui/qt/main_interface.cpp
@@ -702,8 +702,14 @@ inline void MainInterface::showTab( QWidget *widget, bool video_closing )
     }
 
     stackCentralW->setCurrentWidget( widget );
-    if( b_autoresize )
-        resizeStack( stackWidgetsSizes[widget].width(), stackWidgetsSizes[widget].height() );
+    /* A widget shown for the first time has no size to restore (the video
+     * widget asks for its own right after). In minimal view the stack is the
+     * whole window, and an empty size would make the window empty: Qt then
+     * hides it, and on Wayland hiding a window destroys its surface, with the
+     * video's native child still attached to it. */
+    const QSize size = stackWidgetsSizes.value( widget );
+    if( b_autoresize && !size.isEmpty() )
+        resizeStack( size.width(), size.height() );
 
 #ifdef DEBUG_INTF
     msg_Dbg( p_intf, "Stack state changed to %s, index %i",
-- 
